   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Comparative Growing Trials\nAil characteristics and comparisons described below are\nfrom comparative growing trials conducted at Emeratd,\nnear Melbourne, Victoria. Growing conditions were the\nsame as used for commercial production. The plants were\ngrown in a pinebark based medium enriched with time\nrelease fertiliser in a whitewashed poly-tunnel maintained\nbetween 16 and 35\u00b0C in 50% shade. Measurements are\nbased on 20 random selections from these plants, taken in\nJanuary 1991, 3 months after potting on.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
